151:The mango and shrimp salad in the lunch box is bright green, just like bamboo shoots that have just broken through the ground, and the shrimp meat embellishes it with specks of white. As a whole, the colors go well together, and it looks, smells, and tastes good. But that's only if there isn't an enticing deluxe fried chicken rice bowl right next to it.
152:The tragic visual contrast makes me feel even worse about the situation, so I try to eat as quietly as possible to make myself feel more invisible.
153:{character:Kana Fujita}Sigh...
