199:{character:Kana Fujita}Haha, although I'm really happy to be praised by you, it doesn't mean I agree with what you're saying.
200:Kana pulls her loose hair behind her head, then sits down beside me with a glass of warm water. She looks outside the window... The afternoon sun shines through gaps in the shadows of trees, spreading summer to every corner and filling all the gaps between the sky and the earth.
201:{character:Kana Fujita}The reason idols are so popular is essentially that they have something people yearn for.
202:{character:Kana Fujita}Everyone desires to become someone outstanding like an idol, so they start following the footsteps of the other person and start regarding idols as some kind of symbol.
203:{character:Kana Fujita}It might sound a little boastful, but... since I'm lucky enough to become a ray of light in another person's life, I shouldn't do things to disappoint my fans, right?
